WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Read the visitor’s text
name = input("Name: "); User enters Lina; name stores "Lina"
The prompt and the entered response have different roles.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Calculate the badge cost
total = 2 * 4; total = 8
Python uses * for multiplication.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Add the bag fee
total = total + 1; 8 + 1 = 9; total = 9
The right side uses the old total before the update.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Display the stored name
print(name); Screen: Lina
An unquoted variable name uses its stored value.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Display the final total
print(total); Screen: 9
The second print starts the result on the next line.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Read the two result lines
Lina; 9
The entered name appears first, followed by the updated total.
